From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] librados: propagate OTel trace context through reads

The write path already carries a jspan_context across the librados
boundary (IoCtx::operate, IoCtx::aio_operate, Objecter::prepare_mutate_op).
The read path has no such overload — Objecter::prepare_read_op never
sets Op::otel_trace, so MOSDOp arrives at the OSD with an invalid
otel_trace and OSD's "op-request-created" falls back to start_trace(),
producing an orphan trace for every GET.

Add the missing plumbing end-to-end:

  * Objecter::prepare_read_op gains an optional otel_trace param,
    passed to the Op constructor (mirrors prepare_mutate_op).
  * IoCtxImpl::operate_read and IoCtxImpl::aio_operate_read gain
    optional otel_trace params, passed to prepare_read_op.
  * librados::IoCtx::operate and aio_operate gain new public
    overloads that accept const jspan_context* for ObjectReadOperation,
    symmetric with the existing write overloads.
  * rgw_tools.cc::rgw_rados_operate (sync read path) uses the new
    overload to thread trace_info through.

After this patch, RGW S3 GETs produce traces that link the RGW span
to OSD-side op-request-created / dequeue_op / do_op / execute_ctx
spans, the same way PUTs already do.

Signed-off-by: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
---
